body:
> > * Editor-only (TOOLS_ENABLED): if the new resource has no path yet, allow takeover to reconcile stale editor state.
> 
> Can we please not do this? Having core systems behave differently in editor should be considered an Antipattern IMO. In the long run this has a pretty good chance of introducing some obscure and hard to debug "thing xyz does not work in exported game but works in editor" bugs.

Yeah I could see that being an issue in the future. Thanks for pointing that out! 

Would it be better to just have the if statement be:
if (existing.is_valid()) {
			if (existing.ptr() == this) {
			} else if (p_take_over) {
				existing->path_cache = String();
				ResourceCache::resources.erase(p_path);
			} else {
				if (existing->get_reference_count() <= 1) {
					existing->path_cache = String();
					ResourceCache::resources.erase(p_path);
				} else {
					ERR_FAIL_MSG(vformat("Another resource is loaded from path '%s' (possible cyclic resource inclusion).", p_path));
				}
			}
		}
		
And have:

if (p_renames.has(base_path)) {
			base_path = p_renames[base_path];
			r->set_path(base_path + extra_path, true);
		}
		
In `FileSystemDock::_update_resource_paths_after_move`?

Adding true to set_path at least seems to fix the issue.
